      "message": "```\n    /**\n     * Device call state: No activity.\n     */\n    public static final int CALL_STATE_IDLE \u003d 0;\n    /**\n     * Device call state: Ringing. A new call arrived and is\n     *  ringing or waiting. In the latter case, another call is\n     *  already active.\n     */\n    public static final int CALL_STATE_RINGING \u003d 1;\n    /**\n     * Device call state: Off-hook. At least one call exists\n     * that is dialing, active, or on hold, and no calls are ringing\n     * or waiting.\n     */\n    public static final int CALL_STATE_OFFHOOK \u003d 2;\n```\n\nGiven this little documentation about the states I think it\u0027s possible to solve this problem without the redirection service.\n\nThe main problem is taking care of the possible calls combination, I think you must have a per slot callback, but need a global map of slot-\u003estate, so ensure you send the proper slot to the manager",
